# nr-exthost-skill-run: `mixdogd skill-run` (mixdog_skill_scripts::skill_run) replaces skill-script-entry.mjs as the target of mixdog-skill-node.
# Files of this task: mixdog-skill-scripts (Cargo.toml, src/lib.rs, src/run.rs, src/user.rs, src/bin/skill_run_probe.rs, tests/launch.rs) and
# mixdog-mcp/src/launcher.rs (doc comments and its five tests only; the renderers are unchanged). Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave).

## 1. native/core/Cargo.lock
mixdog-skill-scripts gains two unix-only dependencies, both already in the lock and in [workspace.dependencies]: libc, signal-hook.
Regenerate (`cargo update --workspace --offline`); no crate is added.

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
`cargo hakari generate` (signal-hook and libc feature unions for mixdog-skill-scripts).

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-cli/Cargo.toml, [dependencies]
Add (beside mixdog-fsio, optional entries are for features only; this one is plain):
    mixdog-skill-scripts = { workspace = true }
(mixdog-cli -> mixdog-skill-scripts is the new edge; mixdog-skill-scripts depends on mixdog-mcp and mixdog-js, never on mixdog-cli or the daemon: no cycle.)
Dev side, if D:\mixdog-build\tools\unify-test-features.py wants it: mixdog-skill-scripts is listed without features (its `test-support` only builds the probe binary).

## 4. native/core/crates/mixdog-cli/src/main.rs
In `enum Command`, after `EffortJudgeHost { .. }`, add:

    /// The program the `mixdog-skill-node` launchers start: runs a skill script (what skill-script-entry.mjs did).
    #[command(name = "skill-run", hide = true, trailing_var_arg = true, allow_hyphen_values = true, disable_help_flag = true)]
    SkillRun {
        #[arg(allow_hyphen_values = true, value_name = "SCRIPT_AND_ARGS")]
        args: Vec<OsString>,
    },

In `fn main`, after the `Command::EffortJudgeHost { .. }` arm, add:

        Command::SkillRun { args } => {
            // Until nr-exthost-jsrt-skill-scripts: a script that is not shipped runs on the install's bundled interpreter.
            let runtime = match mixdog_app_server_daemon::js_runtime::resolve_current() {
                Ok(js) => mixdog_skill_scripts::UserScriptRuntime::Interpreter {
                    entry: js.package_root.join("src").join("skill-script-entry.mjs"),
                    program: js.program,
                    electron: js.electron,
                },
                Err(error) => mixdog_skill_scripts::UserScriptRuntime::Unavailable { reason: error.to_string() },
            };
            mixdog_skill_scripts::skill_run(args, runtime)
        }

(`OsString` is already imported by main.rs through exec; add `use std::ffi::OsString;` if it is not. A skill script given `--help` or `-x` must reach
skill-run unchanged: allow_hyphen_values on the variant and the argument, and the help flag is off for this hidden subcommand. When the resolve
fails the variant is Unavailable and a non-shipped script prints "<reason>: cannot run <path>" and exits 1.)

## 5. native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose.rs (about line 719)
Replace
    let entry = js.package_root.join("src").join("skill-script-entry.mjs");
    let skill_runtime = ExecSkillRuntime {
        platform: node_platform().to_owned(),
        interpreter: js.program.to_string_lossy().into_owned(),
        entry: entry.to_string_lossy().into_owned(),
        electron: js.electron,
    };
    let skills = SkillRuntime::new(js.program.to_string_lossy(), entry.to_string_lossy(), js.electron);
by
    let mixdogd = std::env::current_exe().map_err(ComposeError::Launcher)?;
    let skill_runtime = ExecSkillRuntime {
        platform: node_platform().to_owned(),
        interpreter: mixdogd.to_string_lossy().into_owned(),
        entry: "skill-run".to_owned(),
        electron: false,
    };
    let skills = SkillRuntime::new(mixdogd.to_string_lossy(), "skill-run", false);
`js` is still used by the extension host. The PowerShell `mixdog-skill-node` function that mixdog-tools exec/invocation.rs prepends to every PowerShell command
renders from skill_runtime, so Windows PowerShell skill calls start `mixdogd skill-run` and not Node. The per-installation launcher directory name is a digest of
the runtime, so it changes with the interpreter and entry (the old directory is left alone).
Other callers that build these two runtimes from the JS runtime (mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/exec.rs builds an ExecSkillRuntime from its caller; search the
daemon and mixdog-cli/src/exec for `skill-script-entry`) take the same two values.

## 6. native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_mcp.rs, ConfigSkillSettings::current
The `jsRuntime` feature (mixdog_mcp::skills::FEATURE_JS_RUNTIME) is on wherever the launcher directory is written (the local daemon and SSH servers alike), so skills
that require it are offered everywhere: after the `for id in ["browser", ...]` loop add
    active.insert(mixdog_mcp::skills::FEATURE_JS_RUNTIME.to_owned());
and, where the server's own settings source builds its `active_features` (SSH server composition), the same insert. Nothing in the daemon inserted it before.

## 7. native/core/crates/mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/js_runtime.rs (not this task's file, for the lead)
`resolve_current()` stays as is until nr-exthost-jsrt-skill-scripts; it is the only consumer of the interpreter variant.

## 8. native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/src/exec/testdata/invocation_node_vectors.json (not this task's file)
Its recorded vectors name `skill-script-entry.mjs`: they are recordings of Node's rendering with a Node-shaped runtime and keep replaying (the renderer is unchanged).
Nothing to change unless the node_cases replay builds its SkillRuntime from compose.rs.

## 9. Test commands (the lead)
cargo nextest run -p mixdog-skill-scripts --features test-support --offline
  (tests/launch.rs: user-script cases run only when MIXDOG_TEST_SKILL_INTERPRETER names a node or electron-in-node-mode binary; the others always run)
cargo nextest run -p mixdog-mcp --offline
cargo nextest run -p mixdog-tools --offline
cargo clippy -p mixdog-skill-scripts -p mixdog-mcp --all-targets --features mixdog-skill-scripts/test-support --offline
